				function rawContent() {
					return "\nCompensation Management in Oracle Fusion HCM enables strategic planning, equitable salary management, and performance-based rewards.\n\n## Compensation Framework\n\nThe compensation framework establishes:\n- Salary structures\n- Grade scales\n- Market positioning\n- Performance linkage\n\n## Salary Structures\n\nDefine hierarchical compensation frameworks:\n\n### Structure Components\n- Grade: Seniority level\n- Midpoint: Target salary for grade\n- Minimum: Entry salary for grade\n- Maximum: Maximum salary for grade\n\n### Salary Grades\nGrades categorize positions by responsibility:\n- Individual Contributor: Non-management roles\n- Supervisor: Team leadership\n- Manager: Department management\n- Executive: Senior leadership\n\n## Market Positioning\n\nAlign internal pay with external markets:\n- Market Data: Industry compensation surveys\n- Positioning: Where you pay relative to market\n- Competitiveness: Ability to attract talent\n- Retention: Ability to retain employees\n\n## Salary Planning Process\n\nAnnual or periodic salary planning:\n\n### Planning Steps\n1. **Analysis**: Review current compensation\n2. **Planning**: Establish merit budgets\n3. **Review**: Evaluate individual performance\n4. **Adjustment**: Propose salary changes\n5. **Approval**: Management authorization\n6. **Implementation**: Apply changes\n\n## Performance-Based Compensation\n\nLink compensation to performance:\n\n### Performance Metrics\n- Goals Achievement: Individual goal attainment\n- Competency Demonstration: Skills and abilities\n- Behavioral Assessment: Cultural fit\n- Business Impact: Contribution to results\n\n### Variable Compensation\n- Bonuses: One-time performance payments\n- Commissions: Sales-based compensation\n- Incentives: Program-based rewards\n\n## Benefits Administration\n\nManage employee benefits offerings:\n\n### Benefits Components\n- Health Insurance\n- Retirement Plans\n- Life Insurance\n- Wellness Programs\n\n## Equity and Pay Fairness\n\nEnsure equitable compensation:\n- Equal Pay Analysis: Gender/demographic pay gaps\n- Variance Reports: Deviation from structures\n- Compa-Ratio: Actual vs target pay\n- Distribution Analysis: Pay spread by grade\n\n## Compensation Reporting\n\nGenerate insights through reports:\n- Salary Summary: Compensation by department\n- Merit Increase Report: Proposed changes\n- Compa-Ratio Analysis: Internal equity assessment\n- Market Comparison: vs. industry benchmarks\n\n## Compliance\n\nMaintain compensation compliance:\n- Equal Employment Opportunity\n- Fair Labor Standards Act\n- State Wage Laws\n- Executive Compensation Disclosure\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Establish clear compensation philosophy**\n2. **Communicate compensation strategy** to employees\n3. **Link to performance** and organizational values\n4. **Review equity regularly** for fairness\n5. **Monitor market changes** for competitiveness\n\n## Conclusion\n\nStrategic compensation management attracts, motivates, and retains top talent while maintaining organizational equity and legal compliance.\n";
				}
